106
00:08:16,940 --> 00:08:19,660
Just how far into the future is this human able to see?

107
00:08:23,520 --> 00:08:31,520
Is this yours?

108
00:08:34,120 --> 00:08:36,460
He sped up my spell and threw it back.

109
00:08:36,460 --> 00:08:46,120
Wow, close call.

110
00:08:46,380 --> 00:08:51,280
Despite my ability to see what you're going to do next, you're too quick on your feet for me to catch up with you.

111
00:08:51,280 --> 00:09:03,340
You know, you'd be awfully helpful to me if you'd surrender right about now.

112
00:09:03,340 --> 00:09:06,700
I wouldn't want to cause any damage to Vongens' body.

113
00:09:06,920 --> 00:09:08,700
So he won't kill me.

114
00:09:09,400 --> 00:09:11,400
He's trying to capture me instead.

115
00:09:11,880 --> 00:09:12,900
He's holding back.

116
00:09:14,000 --> 00:09:16,220
Against me and my four-leaf grimoire?

117
00:09:16,220 --> 00:09:17,700
All right.

118
00:09:18,140 --> 00:09:19,800
Then what must his be like?

119
00:09:20,340 --> 00:09:21,760
And where could it be?

120
00:09:22,720 --> 00:09:25,620
I assume you must be getting curious about my grimoire.

121
00:09:25,940 --> 00:09:28,020
You're welcome to examine it for yourself.

122
00:09:28,300 --> 00:09:29,220
It's right up there.

123
00:09:31,880 --> 00:09:33,600
It doesn't even have a cover.

124
00:09:34,300 --> 00:09:37,100
What kind of grimoire has a bizarre shape like that?

125
00:09:37,100 --> 00:09:40,900
I'm a time magic user with a coverless grimoire.

126
00:09:41,160 --> 00:09:45,400
I never knew whether that was good or bad, but I could tell that it meant I was something special.

127
00:09:46,180 --> 00:09:47,700
I thought hard about it.

128
00:09:48,180 --> 00:09:51,560
And I realized that this grimoire and I have a lot in common.

129
00:09:52,600 --> 00:09:54,920
Neither of us fits into a particular category.

130
00:09:56,060 --> 00:09:57,540
So who am I really?

131
00:09:58,300 --> 00:09:59,700
What am I meant to achieve?

132
00:09:59,700 --> 00:10:03,120
I asked myself these questions for years.

133
00:10:03,580 --> 00:10:06,220
And the more I learned, the more I wondered.

134
00:10:07,100 --> 00:10:10,140
After I'd made it this far, it was finally clear.

135
00:10:10,800 --> 00:10:14,960
The path I'd walked all this way, that is me.

136
00:10:19,220 --> 00:10:21,180
I am the Wizard King.

137
00:10:23,680 --> 00:10:25,740
Yes, I understand now.

138
00:10:26,560 --> 00:10:29,980
What we're planning to do once we have the magic stones

139
00:10:29,980 --> 00:10:33,860
will be an attempt to violate the natural laws of this world.

140
00:10:33,860 --> 00:10:37,740
So this man, this human,

141
00:10:38,520 --> 00:10:42,660
he must have been placed here by fate itself in order to thwart our ambitions.

142
00:10:43,580 --> 00:10:46,320
He is the final bastion of reason.

143
00:10:46,980 --> 00:10:48,620
And as the Wizard King,

144
00:10:49,420 --> 00:10:51,440
I'll protect the people of Clover.

145
00:10:51,560 --> 00:10:53,980
Come what may.

146
00:10:53,980 --> 00:10:55,760
I knew it.

147
00:10:55,760 --> 00:10:57,940
That's all the more reason

148
00:10:57,940 --> 00:11:00,500
why I must end his life.

149
00:11:03,560 --> 00:11:05,000
Protect them?

150
00:11:05,820 --> 00:11:07,240
Go ahead and try!

151
00:11:09,060 --> 00:11:10,300
Sealing magic,

152
00:11:11,300 --> 00:11:11,640
release!

153
00:11:13,860 --> 00:11:16,080
He's expanded his power.

154
00:11:16,080 --> 00:11:24,900
Hey, what's that?

155
00:11:25,400 --> 00:11:26,580
Look up in the sky!

156
00:11:26,800 --> 00:11:28,980
Oh dear, what's going to happen now?

157
00:11:32,920 --> 00:11:35,120
It's absolutely gargantuan.

158
00:11:35,120 --> 00:11:46,380
Humans took away everything.

159
00:11:46,800 --> 00:11:48,120
All of our happiness.

160
00:11:48,660 --> 00:11:50,400
Our friends and loved ones.

161
00:11:51,020 --> 00:11:52,320
Our peaceful days.

162
00:11:52,900 --> 00:11:53,840
Just like that.

163
00:11:54,800 --> 00:11:57,120
It may be an affront to reason,

164
00:11:57,640 --> 00:11:59,440
but you'll atone for your sins.

165
00:11:59,900 --> 00:12:00,760
Now die!

166
00:12:00,760 --> 00:12:13,260
He's been holding on to enough power

167
00:12:13,260 --> 00:12:14,720
to cover the entire kingdom.

168
00:12:15,260 --> 00:12:17,020
Is he going to release all of that magic

169
00:12:17,020 --> 00:12:18,580
and wipe out the whole populace?

170
00:12:19,360 --> 00:12:21,780
I may not be able to kill you,

171
00:12:22,140 --> 00:12:25,320
but I can easily exterminate everybody else.

172
00:12:25,580 --> 00:12:26,960
Whoa, is that magic?

173
00:12:27,920 --> 00:12:29,960
Swords of light, thousands of them!

174
00:12:29,960 --> 00:12:30,820
Look, Mama!

175
00:12:30,980 --> 00:12:32,300
This knife's full of swords!

176
00:12:33,020 --> 00:12:34,280
So bright!

177
00:12:34,700 --> 00:12:36,620
Those blades could kill us all!

178
00:12:37,760 --> 00:12:39,320
Is this how the world ends?

179
00:12:39,660 --> 00:12:40,640
It's unbelievable.

180
00:12:43,460 --> 00:12:45,000
What's that bright light?

181
00:12:45,580 --> 00:12:46,960
It's way over there.

182
00:12:47,640 --> 00:12:49,040
I have a bad feeling.

183
00:12:52,960 --> 00:12:53,880
It's alright.

184
00:12:53,880 --> 00:12:56,540
Even if it turns out to be something dangerous,

185
00:12:57,140 --> 00:12:59,540
we'll always have the brave magic knights

186
00:12:59,540 --> 00:13:00,960
to guard the Clover Kingdom.

187
00:13:05,460 --> 00:13:07,460
The big hunk of light magic.

188
00:13:08,320 --> 00:13:08,920
Damn it.

189
00:13:09,760 --> 00:13:11,540
What the hell is this, Julius?

190
00:13:12,560 --> 00:13:13,620
I gotta hurry!

191
00:13:13,620 --> 00:13:20,880
His spell's already covering everything in sight

192
00:13:20,880 --> 00:13:22,320
at this rate.

193
00:13:23,340 --> 00:13:24,100
Now.

194
00:13:25,100 --> 00:13:27,620
Here is your punishment, humans!

195
00:13:28,520 --> 00:13:29,700
Light magic!

196
00:13:30,480 --> 00:13:31,860
Arrows of judgment!

197
00:13:31,860 --> 00:13:43,880
I did have my doubts.

198
00:13:45,780 --> 00:13:46,220
Honestly,

199
00:13:46,440 --> 00:13:48,960
why do the regular folk have such pathetic magic

200
00:13:48,960 --> 00:13:50,340
compared to people like us?

201
00:13:50,460 --> 00:13:51,580
I couldn't agree more.

202
00:13:51,680 --> 00:13:52,580
To tell you the truth,

203
00:13:52,700 --> 00:13:55,280
I'm not sure why commoners exist in the first place.

204
00:13:55,380 --> 00:13:57,440
We shouldn't have to share the same country with them.

205
00:13:57,540 --> 00:13:58,620
I'll drink to that.

206
00:13:58,620 --> 00:14:03,580
But is that really true?

207
00:14:04,700 --> 00:14:06,060
What are you looking at?

208
00:14:06,760 --> 00:14:07,200
Nothing.

209
00:14:08,240 --> 00:14:10,120
They had strong magic power,

210
00:14:10,520 --> 00:14:12,280
and yet the only thing they ever used it for

211
00:14:12,280 --> 00:14:14,200
was to selflessly line their own pockets.

212
00:14:14,900 --> 00:14:16,980
Why did these useless mages exist?

213
00:14:18,340 --> 00:14:18,980
I see.

214
00:14:19,080 --> 00:14:21,060
You're that magic knight, aren't you?

215
00:14:21,180 --> 00:14:21,540
Yes.

216
00:14:21,700 --> 00:14:23,240
The one with the strange grimoire?

217
00:14:23,980 --> 00:14:24,700
Well, no matter.

218
00:14:25,400 --> 00:14:25,760
Anyway,

219
00:14:25,960 --> 00:14:26,920
I was about to tell you

220
00:14:26,920 --> 00:14:27,540
there's a merchant

221
00:14:27,540 --> 00:14:29,600
who wants me to give his business a leg up.

222
00:14:30,180 --> 00:14:30,620
Really?

223
00:14:31,180 --> 00:14:31,580
No.

224
00:14:31,780 --> 00:14:32,440
We'll talk.

225
00:14:33,300 --> 00:14:34,720
I can't wait to hear.

226
00:14:37,440 --> 00:14:39,940
I kept fighting in my magic knight squad,

227
00:14:40,600 --> 00:14:42,520
hoping I'd eventually discover my calling.

228
00:14:43,520 --> 00:14:44,540
Then, one day...

229
00:14:45,540 --> 00:14:46,600
Go, go, please.

230
00:14:46,680 --> 00:14:47,180
Let him go!

231
00:14:49,400 --> 00:14:50,780
Give me all your yule

232
00:14:50,780 --> 00:14:52,360
or I'll bash your face in.

233
00:14:54,740 --> 00:14:55,460
Hold it!

234
00:14:56,460 --> 00:14:59,040
You villains are always disturbing the peace,

235
00:14:59,200 --> 00:15:00,720
and I'm fed up with it.

236
00:15:01,680 --> 00:15:02,720
